cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "HelixMap-JS: Hierarchical Admixture & PCA Stability Lab"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file (and the Zenodo DOI once available)."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "David"
    alias: "DavidH789"
    website: "https://github.com/DavidH789"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DavidH789/helixmap-js"
url: "https://github.com/DavidH789/helixmap-js"
abstract: >-
  Browser-only hierarchical admixture and PCA stability lab for consumer
  raw DNA (23andMe, AncestryDNA, MyHeritage). Computes continent → region →
  population model contributions with quality-weighted reference frequencies
  (REAL 1000G, literature, blends), LD-pruned frequency PCA, and real 1000G
  hold-out / LOO benchmarks. All processing is client-side.
keywords:
  - admixture
  - PCA
  - population genetics
  - 1000 Genomes
  - consumer genomics
  - browser
  - open science
